{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.complete_minimal_clasp_per_nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.complete_minimal_clasp_per_nucleon","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L128-L136","doc":"Per-nucleon coordination of the complete minimal-clasp cluster is `z = A − 1`\n(`coordinationUnits · 2 / A`), for `A ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.complete_minimal_clasp_coordination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.complete_minimal_clasp_coordination","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L114-L126","doc":"**Complete graph of minimal single-clasp bonds.** If the `A`-nucleon carrier is the complete\ngraph in which every one of the `C(A,2)` pairs is a single minimal clasp (two inter-component\ncrossings), the inter-component crossing count is `2·C(A,2)`, so the coordination count is\n`C(A,2) = A(A−1)/2` and the per-nucleon coordination is `z = A − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.coordinationUnits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.coordinationUnits","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**Coordination units = ½ · (inter-component crossing count).** One coordination unit per clasp;\na clasp is two inter-component crossings (a minimal Brunnian bond, `n₊ = n₋ = 1`). This is the\ngeneral crossing-count → coordination coefficient — no minimal-bond restriction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.interCrossingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.interCrossingCount","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L102-L105","doc":"The number of inter-component crossings of the assembled diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding_indep_of_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding_indep_of_self","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**Binding sees only inter-component structure.** Two assemblies with the same inter-component\ncrossings and mutual energies have equal binding, whatever their self-crossings — the falsifiable\nform of \"binding is purely the mutual pairing.\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**R2 — binding is exactly the (negative of the) mutual pairing.** The self energies cancel: rest\nmass is the self part, binding is the inter-component mutual part. The assignment mass ↔ self,\nbinding ↔ mutual is a theorem of the crossing partition plus the mass-deficit definition, not a\nmodelling postulate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.binding","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L72-L78","doc":"Binding energy, by the standard mass-deficit definition: the sum of the isolated component\nmasses (each = that component's self energy, since an isolated component has no inter-component\ncrossings) minus the assembled mass. Here the sum of isolated masses is `selfEnergy` (the self\ncrossings are exactly those present in isolation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.assemblyEnergy_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.assemblyEnergy_partition","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L63-L70","doc":"**The crossing partition.** Every crossing of the assembled diagram is either self\n(intra-component) or mutual (inter-component), so the total energy splits exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.assemblyEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.assemblyEnergy","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L59-L61","doc":"Total energy of the assembled diagram: the sum over all its crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.mutualEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.mutualEnergy","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L54-L57","doc":"Mutual (inter-component) energy: the sum over inter-component crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.selfEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition.selfEnergy","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfMutualPartition.lean#L49-L52","doc":"Self (intra-component) energy: the sum over crossings that are NOT inter-component. ","signatureChunk":0}]}